 {
  "id": "TS3004b.sys.s.10",
  "text": "The product scope was clarified as a TV remote only, addressing ambiguity between universal remote and TV remote. The team flagged feasibility concerns, noting a proposed price around 25 EUR may be high relative to a production cost of 12.5 EUR. Key design decisions were set: no LCD or speech recognition due to budget, an elderly-friendly, simple layout with large buttons, top-accessible buttons, no two-level navigation, teletext skipped, and a red LED plus a brief under-key lighting indicator. A tight market timeline was identified as a risk, with action item that Paul Wiezer will present the next item after this meeting.",
  "type": "abstract",
  "reference": [
   {
